# One JSON object per line, in the golden format from Part B.5 of the implementation plan. "expect" is "pass", "review", or "block". "rules" lists every rule id from references/00-universal-baseline.md that must appear in the hits for a block or review golden. A pass golden carries no "rules" key. "register" and "profile" are optional per-line overrides, and the CLI default is used otherwise. Copy these three lines as a starting skeleton, then replace text and rules with examples drawn from the approved BAD and GOOD passages in 02-corrective.md.
{"id": "example-block-001", "text": "Importantly, the results held across every condition tested.", "expect": "block", "rules": ["STANCE_OPENER"], "note": "stance adverbial opener"}
{"id": "example-review-001", "text": "That said, the results held across every condition tested.", "expect": "review", "rules": ["HEDGE_CONNECTIVE"], "note": "hedge connective, review by default, block if register.hedge_connectives is set to block"}
{"id": "example-pass-001", "text": "Two respects: the cost and the time.", "expect": "pass", "note": "colon after a number introduces a list, not an announcement"}
